  "status": "data-ready",
  "fetchedAt": "2026-05-23",
  "notes": [
    "HIJRI-UMM-AL-QURA-DATA-STAGE-A1 (2026-05-23) — table extracted from @tabby_ai/hijri-converter v1.0.5 (MIT). See sourceMeta for provenance chain.",
    "TABLE-based — every month length is explicit data, NOT a formula. The site's pages still use the OLD Kuwaiti tabular algorithm until Stage B explicitly switches them.",
    "Year-length anomalies (353-day years): 1356 and 1401. These are real values per the upstream Saudi reference table; they likely reflect mid-year Saudi calendar adjustments. Cross-check against ummulqura.org.sa is PENDING before Stage B can flip the algorithm.",
    "Month-length anomaly: 1364-08 (Shaban 1364, ~1945-08/09 CE) = 28 days. The upstream package contains this value — it is NOT an extraction error. Highly unusual for Umm al-Qura (typical lengths are 29 or 30) and almost certainly reflects a historical Saudi mid-month adjustment. Cross-check PENDING before Stage B.",
    "1447 is a 355-day year (leap by length convention) per Umm al-Qura. The extra day is in Rabi al-Akhir (M4=30 days), NOT in Dhul Hijjah (M12=29 days). This differs from the Kuwaiti tabular algorithm currently used by the site, which always places the leap day in Dhul Hijjah.",
    "Attribution (MIT): This data is extracted from @tabby_ai/hijri-converter (Copyright Tabby FZ-LLC 2023), itself a TypeScript port of mhalshehri/hijri-converter (Copyright Mohammed H Alshehri 2018). Both upstream are MIT licensed. A copy of the MIT notice ships with any artefact that bundles this data.",
    "HIJRI-UMM-AL-QURA-DATA-DISCLOSURE-A1B (2026-05-23): The 1356-1401 AH historical range follows the @tabby_ai/hijri-converter / mhalshehri table interpretation. Cross-check against hijri-core showed differences in parts of this early historical range, including 1356 AH, 1401 AH, and 1364-08. The modern range 1402-1500 AH matches the secondary source fully in the audit, and 1447 AH cross-checks successfully. These early historical anomalies are retained as source-table values and documented rather than normalized to a tabular pattern. See reports/hijri-umm-al-qura-anomaly-crosscheck-1.md for the full audit."
  ],
